{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016aetJwAhjghZ8N9c6VUPZr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the research project carefully to define three tiers for the Dream simulation.\n\nKey facts from the data:\n- Project: recovery_aware_struct_prune\n- Core claim: GRPO fails on structurally pruned reasoning models (reward hacking + collapse), and there's a Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff\n- Model: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B at 20% structured sparsity\n- Second model: Qwen2.5-Math-7B (cross-model validation attempted)\n\nCurrent experimental evidence:\n\n\nThe unpruned model shows GRPO's fundamental issue—reward increases without accuracy gains, jumping from 0 to 0.661 while staying at 81.27%. Pruned variants collapse at different rates depending on structure: RASP fails around step 10, Standard around step 60, while unpruned never collapses. The SFT baseline shows minimal difference between RASP and Standard (2.2 percentage points, not statistically significant), and alpha ablation reveals a U-shaped pattern.\n\nAt 25% sparsity, Standard SFT drops to 51.25% while RASP results are still running. Cross-model validation on Qwen-Math-7B shows the RASP advantage nearly disappears—only 1.5 percentage points at 20% sparsity and 1 point at 25%. I'm currently running GRPO experiments on the 25% sparse models, though I'm concerned that the SFT gap isn't statistically significant and the cross-model results suggest the effect might be limited to this specific architecture.\n\nThe critical unknowns are whether higher sparsity amplifies the RASP benefits enough to reach significance, whether GRPO collapse replicates across models like Qwen-Math, and whether the speedup gains justify the accuracy tradeoffs. I'm hoping the 25% sparsity experiments will show clearer separation between methods, but the cross-model weakness is a real concern for generalization. Now I'm tracking the key metrics across sparsity levels—the SFT gap at 25% is looking promising with a 5pp post-prune advantage compared to 4pp at 20%, and the GRPO collapse pattern shows RASP collapsing much faster (step ~10) than Standard (step ~60), which strengthens the main finding if it holds at higher sparsity.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19575,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19575},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59d74445-74bb-47f9-a763-5e76925cdbdf","uuid":"4d63591b-978c-40d3-b9c3-8bd8a000e87f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016aetJwAhjghZ8N9c6VUPZr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"25%稀疏度放大所有效应 + 跨模型复现collapse梯度 → 三条claim全部成立，RASP作为诊断工具的framing完整\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"25% sparsity下SFT gap显著扩大（RASP vs Standard ≥5pp, p<0.05）\"\n      - \"25% GRPO collapse梯度更陡：RASP ≤5步collapse, Standard ≤30步collapse（比20%快2x）\"\n      - \"Qwen-Math-7B复现collapse严重度梯度（RASP collapse显著早于Standard）\"\n      - \"Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff在两个模型、两个稀疏度上一致成立\"\n    number_ranges:\n      sft_gap_25pct_pp: [5, 10]\n      sft_gap_25pct_p_value: [0.001, 0.05]\n      grpo_collapse_step_rasp_25: [1, 5]\n      grpo_collapse_step_standard_25: [15, 30]\n      cross_model_collapse_ratio_rasp_vs_standard: [3, 10]\n      rasp_sft_25_accuracy: [0.54, 0.60]\n      standard_sft_25_accuracy: [0.49, 0.53]\n    narrative_direction: \"原始framing完全成立。三条claim无需调整：(1) GRPO universal failure + pruning-specific collapse confirmed across sparsity levels and models; (2) collapse severity gradient as zero-cost diagnostic validated on second model; (3) Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff is a general principle, not artifact of single config. RASP既是方法贡献(SFT显著优势)又是诊断工具(collapse速度预测pruning质量)。投EMNLP Main，reviewer concerns全有实验回应。\"\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"25%稀疏度部分放大效应但SFT gap仍边际显著；跨模型collapse存在但梯度不如主模型clean → Claim 1+2成立，Claim 3需弱化\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"25% SFT gap扩大但仍边际（3-5pp, p∈[0.05, 0.15]）\"\n      - \"25% GRPO collapse梯度存在但没有20%那么干净（RASP ~5-10步, Standard ~20-40步）\"\n      - \"Qwen-Math-7B GRPO shows collapse for pruned models但RASP vs Standard差异不显著（collapse步数重叠）\"\n      - \"Unpruned GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling在所有配置下稳健\"\n    number_ranges:\n      sft_gap_25pct_pp: [3, 5]\n      sft_gap_25pct_p_value: [0.05, 0.15]\n      grpo_collapse_step_rasp_25: [5, 10]\n      grpo_collapse_step_standard_25: [20, 40]\n      cross_model_collapse_ratio_rasp_vs_standard: [1.2, 3]\n      rasp_sft_25_accuracy: [0.52, 0.56]\n      standard_sft_25_accuracy: [0.49, 0.53]\n    narrative_direction: \"Claim 1(GRPO universal failure)完全成立且是论文最强贡献。Claim 2(collapse severity gradient)在主模型成立但跨模型证据弱化——改为'diagnostic tendency'而非'clean gradient'。Claim 3(Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff)从'fundamental principle'降级为'empirical observation on DeepSeek-R1 family, consistent with but not proven as general mechanism'。SFT gap报告为trend而非significant result。论文核心叙事转向：GRPO在pruned models上的systematic failure + collapse dynamics作为pruning质量的cheap signal。仍投EMNLP Main但需要补充unstructured pruning baseline做fair Self-Healing comparison，且Discussion需诚实承认generalization limitation。\"\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"25% GRPO不显示clean梯度 + 跨模型完全不复现 + SFT gap在所有稀疏度下不显著 → 核心机制性claim不成立，需reframe为empirical failure analysis\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"25% GRPO: RASP和Standard都在≤10步collapse，severity gradient消失（高稀疏度下两者都太脆弱）\"\n      - \"Qwen-Math-7B GRPO不collapse或两者同时collapse（无梯度差异）\"\n      - \"SFT gap在所有稀疏度下不显著（20%: p=0.25, 25%: p>0.1）\"\n      - \"Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff无法被实验区分——CKA-aware选择在所有recovery范式下效果相似\"\n    number_ranges:\n      sft_gap_25pct_pp: [0, 3]\n      sft_gap_25pct_p_value: [0.1, 0.5]\n      grpo_collapse_step_rasp_25: [1, 8]\n      grpo_collapse_step_standard_25: [1, 12]\n      cross_model_collapse_ratio_rasp_vs_standard: [0.8, 1.5]\n      rasp_sft_25_accuracy: [0.50, 0.54]\n      standard_sft_25_accuracy: [0.49, 0.53]\n    narrative_direction: \"Reframe为：'Structured pruning breaks RLVR alignment — a systematic empirical study'。放弃mechanism-level claim (Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff)和RASP作为诊断工具的角色。核心贡献缩减为：(1) 首次documenting GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling（unpruned数据仍是strong negative result挑战Self-Healing）；(2) 首次documenting GRPO training collapse on structurally pruned reasoning models（即使梯度不clean，collapse本身仍是novel finding）；(3) Empirical recommendation: SFT-only recovery for structurally pruned models。RASP降级为experiment中的一个pruning variant而非方法贡献。论文从'mechanism paper'变为'empirical failure analysis + practical warning'。仍投EMNLP Main(Efficient Methods track接受well-executed negative results)，但需要加强writing和framing的novelty justification，可能需要补inference speedup数据证明structured pruning的实际价值来justify研究的practical relevance。\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19575,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19575},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59d74445-74bb-47f9-a763-5e76925cdbdf","uuid":"b8f7dde3-9b0b-4051-8de3-4061ba27356c"}
